// Reference query. Not deployed in any employer environment.
// Title: Directory replication requested by a host that is not a domain controller, or by the wrong account from an Entra Connect server
// Status: untested template
// ATT&CK: T1003.006 (OS Credential Dumping: DCSync); ATT&CK v19.2
// Data sources: Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting, IdentityDirectoryEvents (Microsoft Defender for Identity sensors on domain controllers)
// Licensing assumptions: Microsoft Defender for Identity within the scenario's Defender XDR stack (Microsoft 365 E5), sensors on every domain controller
// Rule ID: DX-06 | Platform: Defender XDR advanced hunting, custom detection candidate | Suggested severity: High
// Tactic: Credential Access (TA0006)
// Answers: detection-priorities.md item 7 (Priority 2); attack-paths.md AP-5 step 4
// Architecture context: IDS-AD, IDS-SYNC, Z-T0, PIP-ID-RISK; residual risk RR-07; risk register R-05
// Fictional scenario: Contoso Regional Health (fictional). Reference portfolio content.
//
// Purpose
//   Replication of directory secrets is a Tier 0 objective with few legitimate sources: domain controllers,
//   and the Entra Connect servers, because password hash synchronization (assumption A-01) needs the
//   Replicate Directory Changes and Replicate Directory Changes All permissions on the AD DS Connector
//   account. This raw-telemetry rule complements the Defender for Identity alert (DX-05) and keeps the
//   documented hybrid pivot visible: the connector account replicating from anywhere other than IDS-SYNC.
//
// Logic
//   1. IdentityDirectoryEvents rows whose ActionType contains the term "replication". Microsoft documents
//      the monitored activity as "Directory Service Replication" and defers exact ActionType strings to the
//      in-portal schema reference, so the term match avoids depending on one exact spelling. Confirm the
//      value in the portal schema reference before saving this as a custom detection.
//   2. DeviceName is the requesting device; DestinationDeviceName is the domain controller that served it.
//   3. Requests from a domain controller are expected. Requests from an IDS-SYNC server by the connector
//      account are expected. Everything else is returned.
//
// Known false positives
//   - A newly promoted domain controller missing from DomainControllers.
//   - A new or rebuilt Entra Connect staging server missing from SyncServers.
//   - Identity backup or directory management products that read secrets through replication; these need
//     a documented exception with an owner and expiry (principle P-5), not a silent filter.
//
// Tuning knobs (let statements below)
//   DomainControllers, SyncServers   lower-case device names as Defender for Identity reports them.
//   SyncConnectorAccounts            lower-case AD DS Connector account names. Express installations
//                                    create an account with an MSOL_ prefix; custom installations use a
//                                    named account (the value shown is a placeholder).
//
// Response notes
//   Treat as a suspected Tier 0 compromise (RR-07) and follow the Tier 0 branch of the identity compromise
//   playbook. Do not disable the Entra Connect connector account without planning for the synchronization
//   outage it causes; contain the requesting host first. If that host is a clinical workstation or a
//   server that clinical systems depend on, the clinical lead sets the timing of its containment (clinical
//   safety gate, ADR-008; playbook decision point D5).
//
// Validation notes
//   Not run against any tenant. Validate in an isolated lab domain: grant a test account replication
//   rights, request replication from a lab workstation, then remove the rights. Expected telemetry: an
//   IdentityDirectoryEvents row for the replication activity with the workstation in DeviceName and a
//   Defender for Identity DCSync alert. Public library: Atomic Red Team tests mapped to T1003.006, selected
//   by the operator (purple-team-plan.md exercise PX-05).
//
// References
//   https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1003/006/
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-xdr/advanced-hunting-identitydirectoryevents-table
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-for-identity/monitored-activities
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/hybrid/connect/reference-connect-accounts-permissions
//
let LookbackWindow = 1d;
// Lower-case device names (placeholders on a reserved TLD)
let DomainControllers = dynamic(["dc01.corp.contoso.example", "dc02.corp.contoso.example"]);
let SyncServers = dynamic(["sync01.corp.contoso.example", "sync02.corp.contoso.example"]);
let SyncConnectorAccounts = dynamic(["msol_placeholder"]);
IdentityDirectoryEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(LookbackWindow)
| where ActionType has "replication"
| extend SourceDevice = tolower(DeviceName), ServingDomainController = tolower(DestinationDeviceName), Account = tolower(AccountName)
| where SourceDevice !in (DomainControllers)
| extend FromSyncServer = SourceDevice in (SyncServers), ByConnectorAccount = Account in (SyncConnectorAccounts)
| where not(FromSyncServer and ByConnectorAccount)
| extend SuggestedSeverity = case(
    ByConnectorAccount, "High: Entra Connect connector account replicating from a host that is not an IDS-SYNC server",
    FromSyncServer, "High: replication from an IDS-SYNC server by an account other than the connector account",
    "High: replication requested by a host that is not a domain controller")
| project Timestamp, ReportId, ActionType, SuggestedSeverity, AccountName, AccountDomain, AccountUpn, AccountSid, AccountObjectId,
    SourceDevice, IPAddress, ServingDomainController, Protocol, AdditionalFields
